course: dictionary
lesson: 4251
title: Grasp: hold it, get it, or be close to it
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Grasp» has a few meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. To grasp something is to take hold of it tightly, as in «grasp the rope». To grasp an idea is to understand it, especially when it is hard.
explain: As a noun, a grasp can be a firm hold, like «a tight grasp on the rail», or a good understanding, like «a good grasp of maths». Look at the nearby words: rail and rope mean holding, while maths and idea mean understanding.
explain: Sometimes «within grasp» means close enough to reach or get. If «Victory was within our grasp», then victory was almost ours. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it fits, you have found the right one.
fact: Grasp can be a verb (grasp, grasps, grasped, grasping) or a noun (a grasp).
fact: To grasp a thing means to take and hold it tightly, like «grasp the rope».
fact: To grasp an idea means to understand it, especially something hard, like «grasp the idea».
fact: «Within grasp» means close enough to get or reach.
fact: «Grasp at straws» means to try anything, even a weak chance, when you are in trouble.
exercise: «Try and grasp the fact that on this occasion we're not arguing with you; we're just telling you.» What does grasp mean here? | To hold tightly | *To understand | To drop | To reach for a thing
exercise: In «Keep a tight grasp on the rail», what is a grasp? | A good understanding of rails | A loud noise | *A firm hold | A kind of staircase
exercise: «Victory was within our grasp.» What does this mean? | We were too far away to see it | *Victory was close enough to get | Victory was lost for good | We had a grasp of victory's history
test: A teacher says, «She has a good grasp of fractions.» What does grasp mean here? | Holding a ruler tightly | Forgetting | Running fast | *Understanding
test: In «The chimp's big toe can grasp too», what does grasp mean? | *Take hold of something tightly | Cook | Shake | Whistle
exam: In «the great ugly cudgel in his grasp», what does grasp mean? | Lost | Painting | *A firm hold | Understanding
